## Data Flow Example

### Execution Lifecycle

```
1. Frontend: User submits signal
   └─> POST /api/v1/zkdefi/oracle/execute

2. Agent Executor
   ├─ Validates signal against policies
   ├─ Converts to contract call
   └─ Submits to RelayerClient

3. Relayer Client
   ├─ Gets nonce for address
   ├─ Submits call to Starknet relayer
   └─ Returns tx_hash

4. ExecutionStore
   ├─ Saves execution with status='submitted'
   ├─ Logs event: 'execution_submitted'
   └─ Returns call_id to frontend

5. Background: TxConfirmationWorker
   ├─ Polls relayer every 5 seconds
   ├─ Detects confirmation
   └─ Updates: status='confirmed', block_number=45230

6. ExecutionStore
   ├─ Updates execution record
   ├─ Logs event: 'execution_confirmed'
   └─ Archives old events (24h cycle)

7. Frontend: User views execution
   └─> GET /api/v1/zkdefi/oracle/execution/{call_id}
       Returns full history with confirmation details
```

